Key Findings:
The average poverty rate in West Java in 2022 was 8.65%.
Indramayu Regency recorded the highest poverty rate at 12.77%.
Kuningan Regency ranked second with 12.76%.
Tasikmalaya Regency ranked third with 12.72%.
Depok City recorded the lowest poverty rate at 2.53%.
Bandung City and Bekasi City followed with poverty rates of 4.25% and 4.43%, respectively.
The findings indicate noticeable socioeconomic disparities among regions in West Java.

